Pages = {277-293},
Abstract = {We identify and analyze an enigma of U.S. Senate procedure. Why does its
   pivotal voter under simple-majority voting prefer that the body makes
   law using super-majority cloture (e.g., the filibuster, or threat
   thereof, within the strictures of Rule XXII)? Using a two-stage game of
   procedural choice and policy choice, we reveal and rationalize the
   Manchin Paradox and explore its implications for super-majoritarianism
   and legislative organization.},
